<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-SMOKE-LOCALHOST-PORT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-SMOKE-LOCALHOST-PORT-001" ;
  triage:title "run_feature_smoke.py hardcodes the direct-peer port 43101, so the localhost smoke stage cannot target an account-local fixture daemon and the RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 live legs cannot be executed without touching the host daemon" ;
  triage:description "Release-readiness on prerelease/v1.4.13 (7e4302d98), atmbench@rand-m5.local, 2026-09-04T06:4xZ, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 GO, executing RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 leg A against the approved isolated fixture (process-spawned account-local 1.4.13 daemon, direct-peer listener on port 43111 chosen to avoid the uid-501 host daemon on 43101, empty trust store): just smoke localhost passes all 10 doctor checks on 1.4.13 but all 10 send/read and ack-required checks FAIL closed at localhost:43101 with no enabled exact mTLS authority, because scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py hardcodes 43101 for peer resolution (line 270, also line 280) and for the localhost doctor URLs (lines 376-377) and exposes no port override (the only ATM_SMOKE_* knobs are ATM_SMOKE_ATM, ATM_SMOKE_ADVERTISED_HOST, ATM_SMOKE_REMOTE_IDENTITY, ATM_SMOKE_REMOTE_TEAM). The smoke therefore never reaches the fixture and cannot prove legs A or B. arch-ctm correctly declined to bind 43101, alter the host daemon, or invent an override. Related product observation, not yet a separate record: the replacement runtime binds the direct-peer listener on 0.0.0.0 with the port taken only from the --direct-peer-port launch flag (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/lib.rs bind_configured_direct_peer_listener), ignoring the bind IP of the persisted peer interface and falling back silently to local listeners on bind failure; on rand-m5 the 0.0.0.0 bind also raises the macOS network permission dialog, which Rand has ruled out (no more daemon UI prompts), so any future fixture must be loopback-only. Consequence: the two loopback live legs of RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 remain unproven; the rand-m5 host daemon must stay at 1.4.10 with its trust store untouched (team-lead ruling 01M1NGH32YF05AM931QJDB77MN). Classification: harness gap, important; blocking only for the TRUST-KEY loopback legs. Candidate resolutions for quality-mgr ruling: (a) an explicit smoke port override (for example ATM_SMOKE_DIRECT_PEER_PORT) honoured at lines 270, 280 and 376-377, with a loopback-only fixture that is reachable without a non-loopback bind; (b) prove the legs by a different sanctioned path that does not need the host daemon. Do not patch the frozen legacy synchronous daemon." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "smoke-harness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-04T06:52:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:RRG-S1 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-04T06:43:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-SMOKE-LOCALHOST-PORT-001/CAND-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RRG-SMOKE-LOCALHOST-PORT-001/CAND-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" ;
  triage:qmgrRuling "quality-mgr ruling 2026-09-04: approved path (a) -- a small explicit smoke-harness override (e.g. ATM_SMOKE_DIRECT_PEER_PORT), honoured at run_feature_smoke.py:270,280,376-377, paired with a loopback-only fixture per the standing rand-m5 bind rule. This is a harness-only change (no product/daemon code, no legacy-daemon touch). Dispatch as a dedicated follow-up branch AFTER PR #1143 merges, not folded into #1143 -- #1143's own scope (RRG-READ-DOCTOR-LANES-001) already reset CI twice this round and this finding blocks only the RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 loopback legs, not #1143 itself. RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 stays open past release with its live legs deferred to that follow-up, consistent with QA-9's standing disposition. The related product observation (direct-peer listener binding 0.0.0.0 regardless of persisted peer-interface bind IP, silent fallback on bind failure) is noted but not ruled on here -- if it warrants a fix, open it as its own triage record; do not fold it into this harness-port fix." ;
  triage:occurrenceClosureNote "quality-mgr occurrence-level closure (2026-09-04, qa-smoke-direct-peer-port-1152-r1): fix/readiness-smoke-direct-peer-port @ 7475fed9e (PR #1152) implements approved path (a) exactly -- ATM_SMOKE_DIRECT_PEER_PORT env override, range 1-65535, SmokeError on invalid input, default 43101 preserved, honoured at every call site (resolve_dns_addresses, remote_resolve_dns_addresses, curl_doctor URL construction and --resolve flags). Independently verified: git diff --stat origin/develop..origin/fix/readiness-smoke-direct-peer-port confirms scripts/smoke/-only + one doc file (3 files, 53 insertions, 10 deletions); grep for 43101 confirms zero remaining hardcoded literals outside the docstring/DEFAULT_DIRECT_PEER_PORT constant; direct pytest run plus mutation-falsification of the range-validation guard confirms the negative-path tests are real, not vacuous. req-qa and ruthless-boundary-qa both returned zero Blocking findings; ruthless-boundary-qa additionally confirmed no crates/atm-http-runtime touch (the separate 0.0.0.0-bind product observation stays correctly out of scope) and flagged only a non-blocking sibling-naming observation (ATM_SMOKE_DIRECT_PEER_PORT vs run_admission_capacity.py's independent ATM_CAPACITY_DIRECT_PEER_PORT) for a possible future harness-consolidation pass. Both occurrences below flipped to fixed/closed at this commit. Finding-level triage:status intentionally LEFT OPEN per fenix's explicit instruction: finding-level closure requires the live RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001 loopback legs on rand-m5. UPDATE (2026-09-04, fenix carrying fenix@rand-m5 ruling 01M1NMZCXV5QM3PWZGYA9Y4Y9H): #1152 is a correct harness fix but does NOT by itself enable those live legs -- two separate product gaps on develop remain: (1) atm-http-runtime's bind_configured_direct_peer_listener hardcodes a 0.0.0.0 bind (DirectPeerTcpConfig has no bind-address field; the only loopback listener is the plaintext IPC one, not an mTLS peer endpoint); (2) the readiness localhost stage's CLI direct-peer dial port is a fixed constant (client.rs, ~43101) with no override, so it always reaches the host daemon -- the path Rand withdrew. fenix is filing each as its own dedicated triage record (product, important, replacement-runtime-only, deferred past release) and will route the fix PR for review. The TRUST-KEY loopback legs remain blocked on THOSE TWO RECORDS, not on this harness fix -- this occurrence closure is correct and unaffected; only the downstream finding-level-closure narrative for RRG-SMOKE-LOCALHOST-PORT-001 needed this correction so it does not imply the harness fix alone unblocks the legs." .

